(1355013, 172748, 35517, '<td valign="top">excellent work onthe makeup.. looks great.. top marks for putting great effort in, also technically good photo.. 8</td>', 'excellent work onthe makeup.. looks great.. top marks for putting great effort in, also technically good photo.. 8', '2005-05-03 07:44:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(1355015, 172401, 27482, '<td valign="top">Personally, I have seen so many of these shots that they have to be spectacular to work for me and while this is pleasing to the eye, it´s hardly spectacular and I also find it a stretch to fit the challenge as it doesn´t affect me at all although I scored like you fit the challenge.  Anyway, not bad at all, good composition and you used a correct exposure time for the flow of the water but it seems a little bit underexposed so maybe 1 stop higher iso or 1 stop bigger aperture would have fixed that (this could just be the fault of the screen I use here at work though).</td>', 'Personally, I have seen so many of these shots that they have to be spectacular to work for me and while this is pleasing to the eye, it´s hardly spectacular and I also find it a stretch to fit the challenge as it doesn´t affect me at all although I scored like you fit the challenge.  Anyway, not bad at all, good composition and you used a correct exposure time for the flow of the water but it seems a little bit underexposed so maybe 1 stop higher iso or 1 stop bigger aperture would have fixed that (this could just be the fault of the screen I use here at work though).', '2005-05-03 07:46:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(1355016, 172870, 27482, '<td valign="top">Not bad, good moment you captured there but the composition could have been better IMHO.  The lower part of the frame doesn´t really have any purpouse I would have tried placing the dog in the lower right corner instead of dead center, I am not sure it would have been better but it´s just a suggestion on how you could have gotten a more pleasing composition.<br/> <br/>Also I would have cloned out or cropped out that shoe or whatever that red object is in the top right corner, it´s out of place and draws the eye away from the main subjects.  Same goes for the yellow dandelion (or whatever that is) close to the center in the bottom of the frame.  <br/> <br/>Anyway, not a bad shot at all but I think you can do better.</td>', 'Not bad, good moment you captured there but the composition could have been better IMHO.  The lower part of the frame doesn´t really have any purpouse I would have tried placing the dog in the lower right corner instead of dead center, I am not sure it would have been better but it´s just a suggestion on how you could have gotten a more pleasing composition. Also I would have cloned out or cropped out that shoe or whatever that red object is in the top right corner, it´s out of place and draws the eye away from the main subjects.  Same goes for the yellow dandelion (or whatever that is) close to the center in the bottom of the frame.   Anyway, not a bad shot at all but I think you can do better.', '2005-05-03 07:48:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(1355018, 172909, 22011, '<td valign="top">Bubbles are hard to capture, and you''ve done that well, but I''m not really seeing a mood in this photo..  Happiness maybe?</td>', 'Bubbles are hard to capture, and you''ve done that well, but I''m not really seeing a mood in this photo..  Happiness maybe?', '2005-05-03 07:48:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(1355020, 172713, 27482, '<td valign="top">Nice sky with good colours and very pleasing to the eye but needs something extra to make it go "pow!".  Still one of the better shots in the challenge, gave it a 7.</td>', 'Nice sky with good colours and very pleasing to the eye but needs something extra to make it go "pow!".  Still one of the better shots in the challenge, gave it a 7.', '2005-05-03 07:49:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(1355021, 173048, 22011, '<td valign="top">?  he looks bored, but not sad.<br/> <br/>You''ve got the chap in focus well, and exposure is bang on, but the background is really distracting. <br/> <br/>Yes, I know it''s the context for the photo, but I think a more shallow depth of field, or getting in closer would have made this a better shot.</td>', '?  he looks bored, but not sad. You''ve got the chap in focus well, and exposure is bang on, but the background is really distracting.  Yes, I know it''s the context for the photo, but I think a more shallow depth of field, or getting in closer would have made this a better shot.', '2005-05-03 07:51:08.000000', NULL, 1),
